  "notes": [
    "This diocese's cycle names congregations by deanery for the first ~33 weeks (January 4 - August 16), then shifts for the rest of the year to institutional/thematic intercessions (Province Five dioceses, General Convention bodies, diocesan agencies, commissions, retired clergy, diocesan institutions, ecumenical partners) with no named congregations. Both halves are transcribed as printed.",
    "Every week also names two Companion Diocese congregations (Diocese of Southeast Mexico and Diocese of Renk, South Sudan) -- recorded as `category` subjects rather than `parish`, since they are not domestic congregations of this diocese. On August 9 and 16, the source names the companion dioceses generally with no specific congregations that week; transcribed as printed.",
    "January 11: 'Incarnation and, St. Luke's Philippine Independent Church in Bloomingdale' is transcribed as one shared-space congregation entry (a comma after 'and' in the source is treated as an extraction artifact, not a third entity).",
    "August 9: 'Trinity, McHenry (formerly St. Ann in Woodstock, St. Mary in Crystal Lake; St. Paul in McHenry)' is transcribed as a single merged congregation, per the source's own parenthetical.",
    "March 22 and March 29 depart from the deanery pattern entirely with general intercession text (for the spouses/families of clergy and each congregation's own life; and for the diocese, its bishop, and its two companion bishops by name) -- transcribed as `category` subjects summarizing the printed text, with no companion-congregation pairing those two weeks since the source names none.",
    "August 23 - December 27 institutional-era entries have no `parish` subjects (Province Five dioceses, General Convention bodies, diocesan commissions/agencies/institutions, ecumenical partners, etc. are all recorded as `category` subjects, consistent with this diocese's own scope -- `diocese`/`province` subject types are reserved for scope:\"communion\" files).",
    "September 6 names 'Chicago' itself among the Province Five dioceses prayed for that week; transcribed as printed even though it is this diocese's own name.",
    "Campus ministries (Brent House at the University of Chicago; Canterbury House at Northwestern University) and the chaplaincy at Montgomery Place are recorded as `category` subjects rather than `parish`, since they are not parish congregations with a civil place name in the conventional sense."
  ],
